#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mixin_attribute
msgid ""
"\n"
"Abstract building blocks for an Entity-Attribute-Value family: an attribute\n"
"(the dimension being profiled), its values, and a line binding one attribute\n"
"and its chosen values to a subject record.\n"
"\n"
"Ships mixins only -- no concrete models, no data, no views. A consumer\n"
"declares the three concrete models, points them at each other, and inherits\n"
"the coherence rules from here. The pattern mirrors\n"
"``product.template.attribute.line``, generalised so that subjects other than\n"
"product templates can carry an attribute set.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_approval_account
msgid ""
"\n"
"Account Approvals\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"Approval workflow on ``account.move`` through ``mixin.approval``.\n"
"\n"
"Approval triggers, configured per approval category:\n"
"\n"
"* amount inside ``move_amount_min`` / ``move_amount_max``\n"
"* partners listed in ``move_partner_ids``\n"
"* journals listed in ``journal_ids``\n"
"\n"
"``account_move_type`` is **not** a trigger: it only says which kind of\n"
"invoice/bill a creation-flow category produces when the approval is granted.\n"
"\n"
"Per-company settings carry the invoice and bill thresholds\n"
"(``invoice_approval_threshold``, ``bill_approval_threshold``) and their\n"
"required flags. ``move_auto_post`` posts the move once the request is approved.\n"
"\n"
"Requests can also be raised from bank statement lines\n"
"(``bank_statement_line_id``, matched on the request's own statement date and,\n"
"optionally, on already reconciled lines via ``include_reconciled_bsl``).\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_approval_account_l10n_mx_edi
msgid ""
"\n"
"Account Approvals - Mexican EDI\n"
"===============================\n"
"\n"
"Splits the approval requests that create a journal entry by whether their\n"
"journal issues a CFDI (``account.journal.l10n_mx_edi_enabled``): a \"Fiscal\"\n"
"and a \"Non-Fiscal\" filter on the request search view, so the person who\n"
"invoices from approvals can work one pile at a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_approval_res_users_deletion
msgid ""
"\n"
"Account Deletion Approvals\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Where the approval engine is installed, a portal user asking for their account\n"
"to be deleted raises an approval request: who asked, when, and who let it\n"
"through are recorded, and the deletion cron removes only the accounts whose\n"
"request was approved. The shipped category approves self-service requests\n"
"automatically, so behaviour is unchanged until an administrator archives that\n"
"rule and puts a review step in its place.\n"
"\n"
"A bridge rather than a dependency of ``base`` on the engine, on purpose: the\n"
"deletion queue is base's, the engine is optional, and a database that never had\n"
"``approval`` keeps its queue as it was.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_move_template_purchase
msgid ""
"\n"
"Account Move Template - Purchase Integration\n"
"============================================\n"
"\n"
"Extends ``purchase.bill.match`` so ``account.move.template`` records appear in\n"
"the vendor bill Auto-Complete dropdown next to purchase orders and bills.\n"
"\n"
"The three sources share one id namespace in the UNION query:\n"
"\n"
"* vendor bills -- positive ``account_move.id``\n"
"* purchase orders -- negative ``-po.id``\n"
"* templates -- ``MAX(account_move.id) + template.id``, above the live bill ceiling\n"
msgstr ""

