#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_telegram_bot_smart_approval
msgid ""
"===========================\n"
"Telegram Bot Smart Approval\n"
"===========================\n"
"\n"
"Create ``approval.request`` records from Telegram using natural language\n"
"(free text or a voice note). The request is auto-classified into the correct\n"
"``approval.category`` by the AI vendor configured on the bot, and the user\n"
"confirms before it is created and submitted.\n"
"\n"
"This module is the *requester* side of the Telegram approval flow. The\n"
"*approver* side (push notifications and inline approve/refuse buttons) lives in\n"
"``telegram_bot_approval_request`` (task t22525).\n"
"\n"
"Flow\n"
"====\n"
"\n"
"#. User sends ``/solicitar`` and describes the request in text or a voice note.\n"
"#. A voice note is transcribed by the configured vendor, when it supports audio\n"
"   (Groq/OpenAI Whisper, or Gemini inline audio). Vendors that cannot transcribe\n"
"   make the bot ask the user to type instead.\n"
"#. The text is classified into an ``approval.category`` in JSON mode,\n"
"   extracting amount, partner and quantity when present.\n"
"#. The bot shows a summary with inline *Confirm / Change category / Cancel*\n"
"   buttons. When AI is off, fails, or confidence is low, it shows a manual\n"
"   category picker instead.\n"
"#. On confirmation, an ``approval.request`` is created as the requesting user\n"
"   and submitted with ``action_confirm()``. Approvers are resolved\n"
"   automatically by the ``approval.category`` configuration.\n"
"#. ``/cancelarsolicitud`` aborts an in-progress request.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Per-bot, on the ``telegram.bot`` form (**Smart Approval** tab):\n"
"\n"
"* ``smart_approval_ai_enabled`` — master switch. Off by default; the flow then\n"
"  uses the manual category picker (no external API call).\n"
"* ``smart_approval_ai_provider`` — which vendor answers. Defaults to ``groq``.\n"
"* ``smart_approval_ai_model`` — optional model override; empty uses the vendor\n"
"  default. Set it when a vendor retires the default shipped here, which happens\n"
"  fast on some of them (Kimi runs several live model ids with no stable alias).\n"
"* ``smart_approval_ai_credential_id`` — encrypted ``credential.credential`` with\n"
"  that vendor's API key (category *API Key* or *Bearer Token*).\n"
"\n"
"Also register ``/solicitar`` and ``/cancelarsolicitud`` in the bot's\n"
"*Commands*. The commands are available only to chats linked to an internal\n"
"``res.users`` (via ``res.partner.telegram_username``).\n"
"\n"
"System parameter:\n"
"\n"
"* ``smart_approval.confidence_threshold`` — minimum classification confidence to\n"
"  auto-accept (default ``0.75``); below it, the manual picker is shown.\n"
"\n"
"Notes\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"* **AI provider**: swappable per bot, declared in the base module's\n"
"  ``telegram_bot/tools/ai_provider.py`` and shared with the other bots. Two\n"
"  wire families cover every vendor —\n"
"  OpenAI-compatible ``/chat/completions`` (Groq, Gemini's compat layer, OpenAI,\n"
"  DeepSeek, Moonshot/Kimi) and Anthropic's ``/v1/messages``. Adding a vendor that\n"
"  speaks either wire is a ``PROVIDERS`` entry, not a code change.\n"
"* **Audio is a separate capability**, not a property of the chat wire: Groq and\n"
"  OpenAI expose Whisper, Gemini takes base64 audio inline in\n"
"  ``generateContent``, and DeepSeek, Moonshot and Anthropic cannot transcribe.\n"
"  The bot form warns when the selected vendor has no audio.\n"
"* **Vendor quirks are data, not code.** Each vendor entry may carry ``extra``\n"
"  (body overrides applied last, so the vendor beats the caller), ``min_max_tokens``\n"
"  (floor for the token cap) and ``chat_timeout``. Every one of those keys exists\n"
"  because a live probe demanded it: Kimi rejects any ``temperature`` other than\n"
"  ``1``, and reasoning models bill their thinking against ``max_tokens``, so a\n"
"  cap tuned for a non-reasoning model comes back empty with\n"
"  ``finish_reason=length``.\n"
"* **Verified vendors** (probed against live keys, 2026-07-28): ``groq`` (in\n"
"  production), ``gemini`` (chat **and** audio round-trip) and ``moonshot``\n"
"  (chat). ``openai``, ``deepseek`` and ``anthropic`` are wired from\n"
"  vendor-documented shapes but never exercised — treat their first run as a\n"
"  smoke test.\n"
"* **Latency differs by an order of magnitude**: measured on the same\n"
"  classification, Gemini flash-lite answered in ~1s and Kimi k3 in ~19s. The\n"
"  user is waiting in a chat, so prefer a fast model unless accuracy demands\n"
"  otherwise.\n"
"* **i18n**: bot messages are authored directly in Spanish (the base\n"
"  ``telegram_bot`` translator is the identity function), so no ``.po`` is\n"
"  shipped.\n"
"* **Known limitation**: when a required category field cannot be extracted, the\n"
"  bot surfaces the validation error and lets the user change category or cancel;\n"
"  per-field editing in chat is not implemented — complete the request in Odoo\n"
"  web if needed.\n"
"\n"
"Dependencies\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"* ``telegram_bot`` — webhook, dispatch, messaging, inline keyboards, file download\n"
"* ``telegram_bot_approval`` — ``telegram_data`` field on ``approval.request``\n"
"* ``approval`` — the approval workflow\n"
"* ``credential`` — encrypted AI vendor credential\n"
"\n"
"See the implementation plan\n"
"``knowledge/agromarin-knowledge/plans/2026-06-12-t22887-plan.md``.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_telegram_bot_approval_request
msgid ""
"==============================\n"
"Telegram Bot Approval Request\n"
"==============================\n"
"\n"
"Approver side of the Telegram approvals flow. When an ``approval.request``\n"
"reaches an approver, the bot **pushes** it to their chat and lets them\n"
"**approve**, **request changes** or **refuse** (with a comment) straight from\n"
"inline buttons — no slash commands. Browsing all pending requests is handled by\n"
"a **Mini App** (web view) opened from the bot's chat menu button.\n"
"\n"
"Complementary to ``telegram_bot_smart_approval`` (the requester side, which\n"
"creates the request from natural language / voice). Together they move the full\n"
"approval round-trip to Telegram.\n"
"\n"
"How it works\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"- **Push** — ``approval.approver._create_activity`` is extended; whenever an\n"
"  approver becomes *pending* (initial submit or a sequential-chain promotion),\n"
"  ``telegram.approval.notifier`` resolves the approver's linked\n"
"  ``telegram.chat`` (on a bot with **Notify Approval Requests** enabled) and\n"
"  sends a summary with inline buttons.\n"
"- **Approve** — one tap → ``approval.request.action_approve(approver=...)``,\n"
"  attributed to the real approver.\n"
"- **Refuse** — pick a reason (``approval.refusal.reason`` for the category) +\n"
"  optional comment → writes ``refusal_reason_id`` / ``refusal_note`` →\n"
"  ``action_refuse(skip_wizard=True)``.\n"
"- **Request changes** — pick the field (date / description) + comment →\n"
"  ``action_request_change(skip_wizard=True, requested_change_field=...)``; the\n"
"  comment is posted to the owner's chatter.\n"
"- **Mini App** — ``/telegram/approval/app/<bot_id>`` serves a page authenticated\n"
"  with Telegram WebApp ``initData`` (HMAC-SHA256 against the bot token); it\n"
"  lists the approver's pending requests.\n"
"\n"
"Identity is resolved through the chat's ``partner_id → user_ids``; only linked\n"
"internal users can decide. Decisions run on the existing ``approval.request``\n"
"(no public links, no ``quick_approve`` revival).\n"
"\n"
"Setup\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"1. Enable **Notify Approval Requests** on the approval bot\n"
"   (``telegram.bot``).\n"
"2. Link each approver's ``res.partner.telegram_username`` and have them open\n"
"   the bot once so a ``telegram.chat`` is created.\n"
"3. Point the bot's chat menu button to\n"
"   ``<web.base.url>/telegram/approval/app/<bot_id>`` for the Mini App.\n"
"\n"
"Task: t22525.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_bank_dispersion
msgid ""
"===============================\n"
"Bank Dispersion for Odoo 19.0\n"
"===============================\n"
"\n"
"This module provides bank dispersion file generation for payslip runs in\n"
"Odoo 19.0, with full support for the multiple bank accounts and salary\n"
"distribution system.\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"- **Multiple Bank Accounts Support**: Works with Odoo 19.0's multiple bank\n"
"  account system.\n"
"- **Salary Distribution**: Respects percentage and fixed amount allocations\n"
"  per bank account.\n"
"- **Bank-Specific Formats**: Extensible system to support different bank file\n"
"  formats.\n"
"- **Secure Access Control**: Role-based permissions for dispersion generation.\n"
"- **Modern UI Integration**: Integrated with Odoo 19.0's kanban-based payroll\n"
"  interface.\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"1. Place the module in your Odoo addons directory.\n"
"2. Update the app list.\n"
"3. Install *Bank Dispersion for Odoo 19.0*.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Employee Setup\n"
"--------------\n"
"\n"
"- Go to **HR → Employees**.\n"
"- Configure bank accounts for each employee.\n"
"- Use the **Bank Account Allocation** wizard to set salary distribution.\n"
"\n"
"User Permissions\n"
"----------------\n"
"\n"
"Assign the **Payroll Dispersion** group to users who need to generate\n"
"dispersion files.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"1. Create and process a payslip run in **Payroll → Pay Runs**.\n"
"2. Confirm the payslips (state must be ``Done`` or ``Paid``).\n"
"3. Click the **Payroll Dispersion** button in the kanban view.\n"
"4. Download the generated dispersion files:\n"
"\n"
"   - Single file for one bank.\n"
"   - ZIP file for multiple banks.\n"
"\n"
"Adding Bank Support\n"
"===================\n"
"\n"
"To add support for a new bank, implement its generator and register the bank\n"
"under the name (or BIC) it is stored with, in your custom module:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: python\n"
"\n"
"   from odoo import models\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"   class HrPayslipRun(models.Model):\n"
"       _inherit = \"hr.payslip.run\"\n"
"\n"
"       def _dispersion_formats(self):\n"
"           # Keys are matched against the bank's BIC, then its whitespace-\n"
"           # collapsed lower-cased name. Register the full name, not a prefix.\n"
"           return {\n"
"               **super()._dispersion_formats(),\n"
"               \"bank name\": \"_generate_BANK_NAME_dispersion\",\n"
"           }\n"
"\n"
"       def _generate_BANK_NAME_dispersion(self, allocations):\n"
"           \"\"\"Generate dispersion for BANK_NAME.\n"
"\n"
"           Args:\n"
"               allocations (list): List of allocation dictionaries containing:\n"
"                   - payslip: hr.payslip record\n"
"                   - employee: hr.employee record\n"
"                   - bank_account: res.partner.bank.account record\n"
"                   - amount: float (allocated amount)\n"
"                   - sequence: int (allocation sequence)\n"
"                   - is_percentage: bool\n"
"                   - percentage: float\n"
"\n"
"           Returns:\n"
"               str: Formatted dispersion file content.\n"
"           \"\"\"\n"
"           lines = []\n"
"           for allocation in allocations:\n"
"               line = f\"{allocation['employee'].name},{allocation['amount']}\"\n"
"               lines.append(line)\n"
"           return self._prepare_join_dispersion_lines(lines)\n"
"\n"
"Replace ``BANK_NAME`` with the first word of your bank's name in lowercase\n"
"(e.g. ``_generate_bbva_dispersion`` for *BBVA Bancomer*), or use the BIC when\n"
"available — the dispatcher (``_bank_dispersion_key``) prefers BIC over name.\n"
"\n"
"Example Implementation\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"The module includes an example implementation for ING bank that demonstrates\n"
"the file format structure.\n"
"\n"
"Technical Details\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"Key Changes from Previous Versions\n"
"----------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"- Updated for Odoo 19.0's ``hr.version`` system.\n"
"- Support for multiple bank accounts via ``employee.bank_account_ids``.\n"
"- Integration with ``employee.salary_distribution`` JSON field.\n"
"- Modern security system using privileges instead of categories.\n"
"- Kanban view integration instead of form view buttons.\n"
"\n"
"Data Structure\n"
"--------------\n"
"\n"
"Employee salary distribution is stored as JSON:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: json\n"
"\n"
"   {\n"
"     \"bank_account_id\": {\n"
"       \"amount\": 50.0,\n"
"       \"amount_is_percentage\": true,\n"
"       \"sequence\": 1\n"
"     }\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"Troubleshooting\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
"**\"No valid bank accounts found\"**\n"
"   Ensure employees have bank accounts configured and salary distribution is\n"
"   set up.\n"
"\n"
"**\"Bank not supported\"**\n"
"   Implement the ``_generate_BANK_NAME_dispersion`` method for your bank.\n"
"\n"
"**\"Permission denied\"**\n"
"   Assign the *Payroll Dispersion* group to the user.\n"
"\n"
"License\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"OPL-1 (Odoo Proprietary License).\n"
msgstr ""

