#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_mx_partner_blocklist
msgid ""
"Partner Blocklist for Mexican Localization\n"
"==========================================\n"
"\n"
"This module tells you whether a company or person appears on the SAT's\n"
"definitive list of taxpayers under article 69-B, and refuses to stamp a CFDI\n"
"addressed to one of them.\n"
"\n"
"A scheduled action downloads the SAT list every day, replaces the stored copy\n"
"and re-evaluates every contact that carries an RFC.\n"
"\n"
"Configure\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"To be able to download the list you have to set the URL, this can be found in\n"
"http://omawww.sat.gob.mx/cifras_sat/Paginas/datos/vinculo.html?page=ListCompleta69B.html\n"
"and copy the 'Definitivos' URL link into the ``l10n_mx_partner_blocklist_url``\n"
"system parameter.\n"
"\n"
"Access to the list is granted through the **SAT Blacklist Admin** group, which\n"
"the accounting manager group implies: anyone who is an Accounting Manager sees\n"
"the ``SAT Blacklist (Art. 69-B)`` menu and may run the ``Partner Blocklist\n"
"Status`` contextual action. Grant the group to anyone else who needs it.\n"
"\n"
"The module ships that parameter empty, so nothing is downloaded until it is\n"
"set. While it is empty the scheduled action says so in the log at WARNING\n"
"level on every run, along with how long ago the list was last refreshed\n"
"successfully.\n"
"\n"
"Only rows whose taxpayer status is the definitive one refuse a CFDI. If the\n"
"complete 69-B list is configured by mistake, the presumed taxpayers and the\n"
"ones the SAT has cleared are still downloaded and visible, but they do not\n"
"block, and the scheduled action logs how many of them the file carried.\n"
"\n"
"Which statuses count as cleared lives in the\n"
"``l10n_mx_partner_blocklist_cleared_statuses`` system parameter, a\n"
"comma-separated list matched lower-cased and stripped. It ships as\n"
"``presunto,desvirtuado,sentencia favorable``. It is a parameter rather than\n"
"code because the SAT owns that wording: if it ever reworded the column, every\n"
"cleared taxpayer would start refusing a CFDI. To catch that, each download\n"
"compares the set of statuses in the file against the previous one and logs a\n"
"WARNING when it changes, naming what appeared and what disappeared. A file\n"
"with no cleared rows at all is *not* warned about on its own -- that is the\n"
"normal state of the definitive-only list recommended above.\n"
"\n"
"After that the Schedule Action 'Partner Blacklist Process' will download and\n"
"process the list automatically every day at 09:00 UTC, after the SAT has\n"
"published the day's file. The contextual action 'Partner\n"
"Blocklist Status' is installed with the module and needs no setup; use it to\n"
"re-check a selection of contacts without waiting for the nightly run.\n"
"\n"
"The list view shows when the stored copy was last refreshed and turns red once\n"
"it is older than ``l10n_mx_partner_blocklist_stale_after_days`` days (7 by\n"
"default), so an out-of-date list is visible where it is used rather than only\n"
"in the server log. A list that has never refreshed counts as stale.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"If all the configuration was done you can go to any partner and check if it is\n"
"blocked or not. Every partner will have a color (grey, green or red) point in\n"
"the field Partner Status.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: static/src/partner_blocklist_partner_state.png\n"
"   :align: center\n"
"   :width: 200pt\n"
"\n"
"The grey color means there is no information about that partner or the partner\n"
"VAT is not set. The green color means that the partner is not blocked and the\n"
"red color means that partner is blocked and you should not do commercial\n"
"transactions with that partner.\n"
"\n"
"That state also blocks the CFDI of an invoice addressed to a blocked partner.\n"
"Deleting the blocklist record does **not** unblock the partner for long: the\n"
"nightly run replaces the whole table from the SAT file, so the record comes\n"
"back on the next download. A partner leaves the list when the SAT removes it.\n"
"\n"
"A note on spelling\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"The module, its field and its identifiers are spelled ``blocklist``. The model\n"
"``res.partner.blacklist`` and its table keep the older spelling on purpose:\n"
"the nightly refresh writes some 13 000 ``ir.model.data`` rows keyed on that\n"
"literal string, so renaming it is a separate, deliberate migration rather than\n"
"a side effect of tidying the identifiers.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on\n"
"`GitHub Issues <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us smashing it by providing a detailed and\n"
"welcomed feedback.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Originally written by Vauxoo; maintained in this fork by Agro-Marin.\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"* Luis Torres <luis_t@vauxoo.com> (reviewer)\n"
"* Germana Oliveira <germana@vauxoo.com> (developer)\n"
"\n"
"Maintainer\n"
"==========\n"
"\n"
"  .. figure:: https://www.agromarin.mx/logo.png\n"
"     :alt: Agro-Marin\n"
"     :target: https://www.agromarin.mx\n"
msgstr ""

